    "question": "What is cross-validation and why is it useful?",
    "slug": "ai-engineer-what-is-cross-validation-and-why-is-it-useful-10",
    "shortDescription": "Source Question AI Engineer interview question.",
    "sampleAnswer": "Cross-validation repeatedly splits the available development\ndata into training and validation portions so that performance is\nevaluated across multiple splits. In k-fold cross-validation, the data\nis divided into k folds and each fold serves as validation once.\n\nIt reduces dependence on one arbitrary split and is useful for model\ncomparison and hyperparameter selection, especially with limited data.\nFor time-dependent data, ordinary random folds can leak future\ninformation, so time-aware validation should be used instead. Grouped\ndata may also require group-aware splitting.",
    "detailedAnswer": "Cross-validation repeatedly splits the available development\ndata into training and validation portions so that performance is\nevaluated across multiple splits. In k-fold cross-validation, the data\nis divided into k folds and each fold serves as validation once.\n\nIt reduces dependence on one arbitrary split and is useful for model\ncomparison and hyperparameter selection, especially with limited data.\nFor time-dependent data, ordinary random folds can leak future\ninformation, so time-aware validation should be used instead. Grouped\ndata may also require group-aware splitting.\n\nExample : Example: A decision tree reaches 99% training accuracy but\nonly 72% validation accuracy. The team tests shallower trees with\ncross-validation and finds that a depth-limited model gives 86%\nvalidation accuracy, indicating better generalization.\n\nInterview Tip : Give a direct definition first, then explain the\nmechanism, trade-offs, and one practical example. Avoid listing\nbuzzwords without explaining why you would choose them.\n\nWhat Interviewer Is Testing : Conceptual correctness, ability to explain\nfundamentals clearly, and understanding of when the concept matters in a\nreal ML/AI system.\n\nKey Points to Remember : Define the concept precisely, explain the\npractical reason it matters, and connect the answer to measurable system\nor model behavior.\n\nCommon Follow-up Questions : - Can you give a practical example? - What\nare the main limitations or failure modes? - When would you choose an\nalternative approach?\n\nCommon Mistakes : - Giving a memorized definition without explaining the\npractical implication. - Claiming a metric, architecture, or model\nchoice is universally best without stating the assumptions. - Ignoring\ndata leakage, security, evaluation, latency, or cost when discussing a\nproduction AI system.",
