    "question": "What is the bias-variance trade-off?",
    "slug": "ai-engineer-what-is-the-bias-variance-trade-off-11",
    "shortDescription": "Source Question AI Engineer interview question.",
    "sampleAnswer": "Bias describes error from overly restrictive assumptions in the\nmodel; variance describes sensitivity to the particular training sample.\nHigh bias is commonly associated with underfitting, while high variance\nis commonly associated with overfitting.\n\nIncreasing model complexity can reduce bias but increase variance.\nRegularization, more data, feature engineering, and appropriate model\nselection can shift this balance.\n\nIn an interview, emphasize that the goal is not to minimize bias or\nvariance independently. The practical goal is low generalization error\non the target distribution.",
