    "question": "What is a vector database?",
    "slug": "ai-engineer-what-is-a-vector-database-13",
    "shortDescription": "Source Question AI Engineer interview question.",
    "sampleAnswer": "A vector database stores and retrieves high-dimensional vectors\nefficiently, usually using an approximate nearest-neighbor index rather\nthan scanning every vector for every query. It commonly stores metadata\nalongside vectors so retrieval can be filtered by tenant, document type,\npermissions, date, or other constraints.\n\nIn an AI application, a typical flow is: generate an embedding for a\nquery, retrieve similar stored vectors, apply metadata filtering or\nreranking if needed, and pass the best evidence to the downstream model.\n\nThe database is an infrastructure component; it does not automatically\nguarantee semantic quality. Embedding quality, chunking, indexing,\nfiltering, and evaluation still matter.",
