    "question": "What is a context window?",
    "slug": "ai-engineer-what-is-a-context-window-20",
    "shortDescription": "Source Question AI Engineer interview question.",
    "sampleAnswer": "A context window is the maximum amount of tokenized information\na model can process as context for a request, subject to the model’s\nspecific limits. It can include system instructions, conversation\nhistory, retrieved documents, tool results, and the requested output\ndepending on the API/model behavior.\n\nA larger context window does not automatically mean better answers.\nExcessive or low-quality context can increase cost, latency, and\ndistraction. Good AI systems therefore retrieve and compress relevant\ninformation instead of blindly placing every available document into the\nprompt.",
