    "question": "What do temperature and top-p control?",
    "slug": "ai-engineer-what-do-temperature-and-top-p-control-21",
    "shortDescription": "Source Question AI Engineer interview question.",
    "sampleAnswer": "Temperature controls how sharply or broadly the model samples\nfrom its next-token probability distribution. Lower temperature\ngenerally makes output more deterministic; higher temperature generally\nincreases variability.\n\nTop-p, or nucleus sampling, restricts sampling to the smallest set of\ntokens whose cumulative probability reaches a chosen threshold. Lower\ntop-p narrows the candidate set.\n\nThey are sampling controls, not direct “intelligence” controls. For\ndeterministic business workflows, low randomness is often preferred; for\ncreative generation, more variability may be useful. The exact effect\ndepends on the model and serving implementation.",
