    "slug": "ai-engineer-what-is-the-difference-between-a-base-model-and-an-instruction-tuned-model-22",
    "shortDescription": "Source Question AI Engineer interview question.",
    "sampleAnswer": "A base model is primarily trained to model language or continue\ntext from large-scale pretraining data. An instruction-tuned model\nreceives additional training to follow user instructions and produce\nresponses in a desired conversational or task-oriented format.\n\nInstruction tuning generally makes a model easier to use for\nassistant-style tasks, while a base model can be useful for specialized\ntraining or applications that need different behavior.\n\nIn practice, the correct choice depends on the serving API, fine-tuning\napproach, task, and evaluation results rather than assuming\ninstruction-tuned always means better for every workload.",
