    "slug": "ai-engineer-how-would-you-choose-a-chunking-strategy-for-a-rag-system-26",
    "shortDescription": "Source Question AI Engineer interview question.",
    "sampleAnswer": "Chunking divides source documents into retrievable units. A\ngood strategy balances semantic completeness against retrieval precision\nand context cost.\n\nStart with document-aware boundaries such as headings, paragraphs,\nsections, tables, or code blocks rather than blindly cutting every N\ncharacters. Use overlap only when it helps preserve cross-boundary\ncontext. Chunk size should be evaluated against the document type,\nembedding model, query style, and downstream context budget.\n\nFor long structured documents, hierarchical or parent-child retrieval\ncan preserve section context while keeping retrieved units focused.\nAlways evaluate retrieval recall and answer quality on representative\nqueries.",
