    "shortDescription": "Source Question AI Engineer interview question.",
    "sampleAnswer": "Vector search retrieves by semantic similarity, which is strong\nwhen the query and relevant content use different but related wording.\nLexical search, such as BM25, is strong for exact terms, identifiers,\nproduct codes, names, and rare keywords.\n\nHybrid search combines both signals and often works better for\nenterprise or e-commerce corpora containing both natural language and\nexact-match requirements. A common design retrieves candidates from both\nsystems and combines or reranks them.\n\nThe choice should be driven by evaluation on real queries, including\nexact-match and semantic cases.",
